# ============================================================================
# BurnScope .gitignore
# This repository is public. Nothing personal, secret or third-party-licensed
# should be committed -- the rules below are what keeps it that way.
# ============================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- secrets
# Contains GROQ_API_KEY, GEMINI_API_KEY, HF_TOKEN, DATABASE_URL, EMAIL_ADDRESS,
# EMAIL_APP_PASSWORD (a Gmail app password). NEVER commit this file. Commit
# .env.example instead (see README "Configuration").
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
build/
dist/

# Virtual environments (name varies by how each person creates theirs)
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- runtime data (regenerated, or per-user)
# The local case database: real user data. Never commit it.
data/cases.db
data/cases.db-journal
data/cases.db-wal
data/cases.db-shm

# Per-user uploaded photos and per-user generated files (Grad-CAM overlays,
# PDF reports). May contain real photos and reports of real people.
data/users/
outputs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- NOT part of the public repository
# Demo photos: they come from third-party sources (some show identifiable
# people), so they are kept out. Put your own JPGs in data/sample_images/ to
# get the in-app "sample photo" picker and the tests that use them.
data/sample_images/*
!data/sample_images/README.md

# Guidance documents (the RAG corpus): adapted from WHO, national guidelines
# and patient-information leaflets, each under its own licence, so they are
# not redistributed here. See rag/source_docs/README.md for what to supply.
rag/source_docs/*
!rag/source_docs/README.md

# The search index built from those documents (rebuilt automatically on the
# first start, or with: python -m rag.build_index).
rag/vector_store/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Streamlit
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- local notes and tool state
CLAUDE.md
.claude/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*.swo
.idea/
.vscode/
*.sublime-workspace

# ============================================================================
# Deliberately NOT ignored:
#   models/classifier/*.keras, models/segformer/*.pth  (~162 MB combined, stored
#     with Git LFS -- see .gitattributes and README "Model weights")
#   docs/sample_report.pdf                              (an example generated report)
# ============================================================================
